cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GeoEvals, please cite it as below. When you report results, also cite the
  benchmark ID and version, the metric versions and the dataset manifest hash, and cite each
  dataset as its manifest asks.
type: software
title: "GeoEvals: a reproducible framework for evaluating geospatial AI systems"
abstract: >-
  GeoEvals is a reproducible, practitioner-focused framework for evaluating geospatial AI
  systems. It defines versioned benchmark specs, dataset manifests, adapters, metrics with
  explicit units and tolerances, a runner that records timing and cost, and machine-readable
  run results and reports.
authors:
  - name: GeoEvals contributors
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - geospatial
  - GIS
  - evaluation
  - benchmark
  - AI
  - reproducibility
